 "transcript": {
  "answer": "No. Against the yen, the Aussie dollar is strong by recent standards. It has slipped a little in the past few weeks.\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 bought about ¥109.67 on 16 October 2026 (RBA, 4pm).\n- **Past year:** It was about ¥100.84 at the end of October 2025 and ¥91.43 in April 2025. That makes it roughly 9% higher than a year ago and about 20% higher than the April 2025 low.\n- **Recent peak:** It reached about ¥114.3 in April 2026 and ¥114.5 in August 2026. The 2025–26 high I saw in month-end data was ¥114.54 in August 2026.\n- **Past few weeks:** It has fallen about 4% from ¥114.63 on 1 September. It has been steady at ¥109–111 since mid-September.\n\nThe dollar is below its mid-2026 highs, but well above where it was through 2025. These figures are only from January 2025, so I can't say how it compares with longer-term history.",
